!! [[0.12.1|https://crosseye.github.io/TW5-JSON_Convert/0.12.1/]]
//Released 2026-09-29//

The first bug report against the announcement was the editor's own doing: click ''New…'', name a profile, and the first thing on screen was a red box with two issues in it — the validator correctly noting that an empty profile has no records path and no title binding, presented as though something had gone wrong.

* ''A new profile gets a welcome, not a warning.''  When a profile has neither `records` nor `tw-fields`, the editor says what the two things are and where to click, instead of listing them as errors.  The issues banner returns as soon as there is something to check.
* ''New… takes pasted JSON.''  The prompt has a box for a profile's text — from a guide, a forum post, a colleague — so "give it this text" is something you can do where you are standing.  Left empty, it makes an empty profile as before.  Text that is not a JSON object is refused with a hint.
